# Non-secret candidate settings to MERGE into the server .env.
# Target: dual Xeon + RTX4090, six separate station PCs acquiring cameras.
# Each station sends its latest frame; models execute on the central GPU.
# The six-station model recipe is unconfirmed and may use six different models.
# Do not assume three screw and three sticker tasks.
# This is not a complete environment file and is not auto-applied.
REALTIME_BACKEND=yolo
POSE_BACKEND=yolo
INFERENCE_DEVICE=cuda:0
# Start CPU operator pools at 4; do not set them to all 40 CPU cores.
# Change one setting at a time using measured six-station latency/throughput.
# Apply NUMA affinity only after checking and testing the target CPU/GPU/NIC
# topology; this template intentionally prescribes no affinity settings.
OPENCV_THREADS=4
TORCH_THREADS=4
STATION_QUEUE_WAIT_MS=500
# Exactly one API instance and one Uvicorn worker; allow up to three executions.
# Scene concurrency is min(STATION_INFERENCE_CONCURRENCY, REALTIME_POOL_SIZE,
# SCENE_MODEL_CACHE_SIZE): different model keys can run concurrently, while
# the same model instance and each station remain serialized with fair scheduling.
# The default scene cache of 1 below still limits scene concurrency to 1.
# Station frames and /api/v1/realtime/frame share the total admission cap
# min(STATION_INFERENCE_CONCURRENCY, REALTIME_POOL_SIZE), as well as kind caps.
# Collector HTTP/1.1 connections are reused; interrupted POSTs are never
# automatically replayed. A later new request may reconnect with a fresh frame.
# These are candidate capacities, not a guarantee of six-station throughput.
# Current pipeline uses CUDA registration/features, not the early CPU SIFT path.
# Sticker warp_regions and within-frame target batching reduce repeated work;
# cross-stream model batching and lower-cadence person inference are NOT implemented.
# Shared-GPU results varied: validate CPU contention, memory and sustained
# throughput on the target dual-Xeon/RTX4090 server before raising these limits.
STATION_INFERENCE_CONCURRENCY=3
REALTIME_POOL_SIZE=3
SPECIALIST_POOL_SIZE=3
# Station sampleFps is configured per binding, not by this environment file.
# Final user target: 10 EFFECTIVE fps for EACH of six stations, 60 fps total.
# This means a 100 ms sampling period; simply setting sampleFps=10 is not proof.
# Use 4 fps (24 total) then 6 (36 total) as diagnostic stages, not a reduced
# acceptance target. Define P95, result-age and maximum no-result-gap limits
# for each process; total/average FPS cannot compensate for a slower station.
# Unknown models on this RTX4090 host have not been validated at 10 fps each.
# A multi-GPU decision requires actual model/topology/load measurements first.
# Sampling-only edits preserve credentials/current logins; stop the stream first.
# Refresh an open /terminal page or restart its collector to read the new FPS;
# a collector's explicit --fps still caps the binding value.
# Different task/device bindings still rotate credentials. No-op stays unchanged.
# Validate fixed and serial API arrival modes separately; repeated JPEG API tests
# omit capture/encoding/display and do not establish camera end-to-end FPS.
# Local 5070 Ti results, including a single browser's sticker replay at ~6 fps,
# do not validate six station PCs on this RTX4090 host. See
# docs/history/throughput-optimization-2026-11-07.md and
# docs/guides/six-station-realtime.md for measurements and acceptance limits.
# Deploy the DISK feature asset and pinned dependencies; see
# docs/guides/cuda-station-vision.md for migrated scope and accuracy limits.
# Measure each actual model, then budget model residency for their combined load.
# Cache size 1 can evict/reload distinct scene models repeatedly. Raise it only
# after measuring all resident models' VRAM needs; this template keeps it at 1.
# Six measured-to-fit models may use cache size 6, but the global execution cap
# remains 3 here. Loading/in-use models are pinned and cannot be evicted.
# Full/busy cache slots reject new work rather than loading unbounded models.
# Local RTX5070 Ti two-model CUDA smoke matched all 6/6 non-timing outputs
# with distinct workers/streams (test-results/six-workstation-4090-prep-20261107/
# scene-cuda-smoke.json), but generic scenes still use Ultralytics model.predict:
# installed Profile.time calls self.accelerator.synchronize(self.device), and
# this change leaves its preprocessing/postprocessing/device-wide timing sync
# intact, so host/stream concurrency does not prove full kernel overlap or
# throughput/accuracy acceptance; specialist cuda_yolo has a separate implementation.
# Source implementation and CPU concurrency tests do not establish 60 fps on
# RTX4090; validate the actual six models and edge acquisition end to end.
# Different weights/contracts cannot be combined into one inference batch.
SCENE_MODEL_CACHE_SIZE=1
DB_POOL_SIZE=5
DB_MAX_OVERFLOW=5
# Production sampling gets the GPU; queued offline/training work waits.
# Re-enable both and recreate Worker during a maintenance window.
WORKER_ANALYSIS_ENABLED=false
WORKER_TRAINING_ENABLED=false
